      en: "The Pescanova shrimp farm in Ecuador, operated through its subsidiary Promarisco, is a cornerstone of the global export of Whiteleg shrimp (Litopenaeus vannamei). Ecuador has emerged as the world's leading exporter of these crustaceans, and Pescanova's facilities in Guayas Province are among the most advanced in the sector. The farms employ sophisticated aquaculture techniques where water quality and feeding are precisely monitored to ensure healthy growth without the use of antibiotics. Pescanova integrates the entire value chain, from hatcheries and grow-out ponds to a high-tech processing plant where shrimp are flash-frozen for shipment to Europe and North America. The company prioritizes sustainability and holds ASC (Aquaculture Stewardship Council) certification, ensuring the protection of surrounding mangrove ecosystems. This industry is a massive generator of foreign exchange for Ecuador and secures thousands of jobs in rural coastal areas.",
